  "texts": {
    "preamble": "B.Srinu vs State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5085 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 and A2 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.135 of 2019 of Ongole I Town Police Station, Prakasam District, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 273 and 420 of IPC and Sections 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 29.04.2019 at 10.00 hours, when the complainant along with his staff inspected A1's shop situated at Shop No.G/6, Om Sai Complex, Gurramvari Street, Ongole, found the banned tobacco products in the shop and on enquiry, it came to light that he purchased the same from A2 and A3 and hence, arrested the accused and seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.135 of 2019 of Ongole I Town Police Station, for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "arguments": "",
